<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαυμάσι-ος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θωμ-</span></b> , rarely <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>Im.</u>
			19
		</span></i>: (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαῦμα </span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wonderful, marvellous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					443
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					584
				</span></i>
			 (nisi neut. pl.); [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδὸς] θωμασιωτέρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θωμάσια</span>
			<i>wonders, marvels</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				35
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαυμάσια ἐργάζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					220a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧττον θαυμαστά, καίπερ ὄντα
				θαυμάσια</span> less <i>admired</i>, though
			<i>admirable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.974d
			</span></i>: c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέρας θ. προσιδέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					1.26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ θ. [ἐστι</span>] c.
			inf., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				468
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστιν δὲ . . τοῦτο . . θ., ὅπως . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					340
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. τοῦ κάλλους</span>
			<i>marvellous</i> for beauty, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.3.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν τόλμαν -ώτατε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.152
				</span></i>
			: with interrog., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαυμάσιον ὅσον</span>
			<i>exceedingly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				217a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαυμάσι᾽ ἡλίκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					19.24
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -ώτατον</span> what is
				<i>most wonderful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.63
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>
			<i>wonderfully</i>, i.e. <i>exceedingly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
			</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1240
			</span></i>: freq. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς, θ. ὡς ἄθλιος</span>
			<i>marvellously</i> wretched, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				471a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἂν ὡς ηὐλαβούμην</span> I
			should be <i>wonderfully</i> cautious, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				29.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>disposed to wonder</i>, in Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν οὐ -ίως γ᾽ ἔχουσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>admirable, excellent</i>, with slight irony, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				242a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.113
			</span></i>: freq. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ θαυμάσιε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					435c
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ -ώτατε ἄνθρωπε</span>,
			in scorn, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.1.27
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. καὶ ἄλογον</span>
			<i>strange</i> and absurd, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				496a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαυμάσια . .
			ἐργαζομένους</span> behaving <i>in an extraordinary
			manner</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				35a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
